course: dictionary
lesson: 6129
title: Might: possible, polite or powerful
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Might is a small word with more than one job. Most of the time it means something is possible but not certain: «It might rain later.» You do not know yet, so you say might rather than will.
explain: Might can also be the past of may when you report what someone said: «Kieran tells Connor his dad lost his job and they might move.» It can make a polite suggestion too: «You might try again.» That sounds gentle, not bossy.
explain: As a noun, might means great power or strength, as in «with all his might». To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Is something possible, is someone being polite, or is there a big push or effort?
fact: Might means possible but not certain, so it sits between impossible and certain.
fact: «Might» is a modal verb, like may. It has no -s form, so say «she might come», not «she mights come».
fact: «With all his might» means with great effort or strength.
fact: Phrases to learn: might as well, might have, with all your might.
fact: In maths, words like «might» show that something is possible but not certain.
exercise: «It might rain this afternoon, so take a coat.» What does might mean here? | *Possible, but not certain | Certain to happen, so pack it now | Impossible, the sky is clear
exercise: «Kieran tells Connor his dad lost his job and they might move.» Which word shows the move is only a possibility? | dad | *might | job | lost
exercise: In a story, a hero pushes the door «with all his might». What does might mean in this sentence? | The past of may | Possible but not sure | *Great strength or power | A polite suggestion
test: «You might try again.» What kind of meaning does might give this sentence? | A rule that must be obeyed | A fact about the past | *A polite suggestion | Something that is impossible
test: Which sentence uses might as a noun? | «It might snow tomorrow.» | «You might try again.» | *«She pushed the rock with all her might.» | «She said she might come.»
exam: «Scientists think this might be a bit like dreaming, but it is still argued.» What does might show? | *That it is possible but not proven | That it is a noun meaning power | That it is certain and proven | That it is impossible
